Why Is Demand Increasing?
Expansion of data centers: Cloud computing, artificial intelligence, and growing data consumption are driving investment in facilities that require effective underfloor cable management, power distribution, airflow, and cooling.
Flexible commercial workplaces: Modern offices increasingly need adaptable layouts that allow electrical, data, and HVAC connections to be relocated as workplace requirements change.
Safety and performance requirements: Demand for durable, fire-resistant, and anti-static flooring systems is increasing in data centers, laboratories, healthcare facilities, and other environments with specialized infrastructure needs.

Raised Access Floor Watch: Sustainable Materials and Smart Buildings
The market is evolving toward flooring systems that combine structural strength with improved fire resistance, electrostatic discharge protection, and sustainable materials. Calcium sulphate panels are among the available product categories, alongside steel-encapsulated, aluminum, and chipboard-encapsulated systems. Building Information Modeling and smart-building technologies are also helping project teams plan underfloor infrastructure more efficiently.

