Why This Market Matters
Raised access flooring provides a practical way to manage power, data cabling, and other building services while allowing easier maintenance and infrastructure upgrades. Its role is especially important in data centers, where airflow, equipment accessibility, and reliable operations are essential. However, initial installation costs, complex installation requirements, competing overhead cable systems, and construction-sector uncertainty can affect adoption.

